* START-HISTORY:
* 22 Sep 26 dm - new.  SD_PyListCrte (2220) was reserved in KEYS.H and
*                dispatched by op_sdpyobj.c/sdext_py.c, but nothing in BASIC
*                called it, so a list could be appended to and read but
*                never made - PyListAppd/PyListGet/PyListClr all existed,
*                PyListCrte did not.  Found by the Windows port (RELEASE_1.1,
*                gate 47 audit, 22 Sep 2026 mail) after hitting the identical
*                gap on their own side and fixing it as PY_LISTCREATE, "the
*                21st Python program... shaped exactly like PY_CREATEDICT."
*                Same shape here, our own architecture underneath: PyListCrte
*                (sdext_py.c) uses PyList_New()/PyMapping_SetItemString
*                directly, matching PyDictCrte, not Windows' py_call("LISTCRTE",..)
*                helper-process dispatch - same result, different mechanism.
*                New error codes SD_PyErr_LstCrteEr/SD_PyErr_LstExsts
*                (err.h -12037/-12038), following this tree's own LstAppdEr/
*                LstClrEr numbering (already diverged from Windows's, which
*                has neither).
* END-HISTORY
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
* return_status = PY_LISTCRTE(listname)
*
* listname - name of python list to create
* return_status 0 - success or error as defined in ERR.H
*               status() - 0 on success, error code as defined in ERR.H
*
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
$no.symbols
$no.xref
function py_listcrte(listname)
$catalog !py_listcrte

$include KEYS.H
$include ERR.H

* Reject empty Python object name(s) before SDPYOBJ/SDEXT call, as the
* other PY_* programs do.
if listname = '' then
   set.status 1
   return 1
end
* --------------------
rtn_status = SDPYOBJ("","",listname,SD_PyListCrte)
*
return rtn_status

end
